{"id": "Db3Eg5Khhxg", "title": "Video by krishnachaytanyaa", "description": "VPN explained: what your wifi can actually see, and what it can’t.\n\nHTTPS hides what you send. Not where you send it.\n\nEvery request has a destination on the outside, and your wifi, your\nrouter and your ISP all read it ,that’s how they forward it. The\ncontents are sealed, but the address isn’t. That’s why your network\ncan log github.com, then paypal.com, then whatsapp.com, even though\nevery one of those is encrypted.\n\nA VPN wraps the whole request inside a second one addressed to the VPN\nserver. Now everything on the path sees the same destination, whatever\nsite you’re actually visiting. The server unwraps it and forwards it\nusing its own address, so the site sees the VPN instead of you.\n\nThe part most explainers skip: you didn’t remove the watcher. You moved\nit. Your VPN provider now sees exactly what your ISP used to — which is\nwhy who runs it matters more than any feature list.\n\nSave this for the next time someone says a VPN makes you anonymous.\nFollow @krishnachaytanyaa for backend and system design you can see.\n\n#vpn #networking #cybersecurity #systemdesign #backend", "timestamp": 1786366806, "channel": "krishnachaytanyaa", "uploader": "Krishna Chaitanya | Solutions Architect", "uploader_id": "27131031756", "like_count": 913, "comment_count": 7, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "duration": 8.984000205993652, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1751359252865076a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 64.128, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr20-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQMFdOIRcK-wOiTYw_xdxBgd4Z0fdhYAdTwpQeIm1dKieyl0pD-pJLcw4E_YHcFuEASMiUEclwsDR0YS3Z7npb5xSOlYyLCa_Wb_qAc.mp4?_nc_cat=111&_nc_oc=AdqhW7UExWUBFrW72ZgMioClQAYYghHAM4Dn_f-Rw1kql3FhAccPnAri6h4TC9FWadwEbHrxMz1xV9VChI-VHBzJ&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr20-2.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=Y7JuENh